# 🔍 Multi-Modal Neural Search Engine

**Dense Retrieval · Query Expansion · Cross-Modal Re-ranking · CLIP + FAISS**

---

## 📁 Project Structure

```
multi_modal_search_engine/
├── app/
│   └── streamlit_app.py          ← Web UI (run this to use the search engine)
├── core/
│   ├── text_encoder.py           ← Sentence-BERT text embeddings
│   ├── image_encoder.py          ← CLIP image & text embeddings
│   ├── index_builder.py          ← FAISS index creation and loading
│   ├── search.py                 ← Multi-modal retrieval logic
│   ├── reranker.py               ← Cross-encoder re-ranking
│   └── query_expansion.py        ← WordNet / Word2Vec / PRF expansion
├── data/
│   ├── raw/                      ← Downloaded raw files
│   ├── processed/                ← JSON files used by indexer
│   ├── images/                   ← Image files (Flickr30k / COCO)
│   └── texts/                    ← (optional extra text files)
├── indexes/
│   ├── text_index.faiss          ← Built by build_index.py
│   ├── image_index.faiss         ← Built by build_index.py
│   └── metadata.pkl              ← Doc text + image paths + captions
├── scripts/
│   ├── download_data.py          ← Downloads MS MARCO + Flickr30k/COCO
│   ├── build_index.py            ← Encodes data and builds FAISS indexes
│   └── evaluate.py               ← P@k, R@k, MAP, MRR, nDCG evaluation
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md
```

---

## ✅ Step-by-Step Setup Guide

### Step 0 — Prerequisites

- Python **3.9 – 3.11** (recommended: 3.10)
- At least **8 GB RAM** (16 GB preferred)
- At least **15 GB free disk space**
- GPU optional but speeds up encoding significantly
- Create folders a data and indexes in root folder 

---

### Step 1 — Create and activate a virtual environment

```bash
# Navigate to the project folder
cd multi_modal_search_engine

# Create virtual environment
venv\Scripts\activate
```

---

### Step 2 — Install dependencies

```bash
pip install --upgrade pip
pip install torch torchvision --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu
# (Use cu118 instead of cpu if you have an NVIDIA GPU)

pip install -r requirements.txt

# Install OpenAI CLIP manually (not on PyPI)
pip install git+https://github.com/openai/CLIP.git

# Download NLTK data
python -c "import nltk; nltk.download('wordnet'); nltk.download('stopwords'); nltk.download('punkt'); nltk.download('averaged_perceptron_tagger')"
```

---

### Step 3 — Download the datasets

#### Option A — Quick start (recommended for first run)

Downloads ~5,000 text passages from MS MARCO and ~2,000 images from Flickr30k.
Total download size: ~500 MB.

```bash
python scripts/download_data.py --all --sample 5000
```

#### Option B — Larger dataset for better results

```bash
python scripts/download_data.py --coco --sample 5000    # MS-COCO images
```

#### What gets downloaded:

| Dataset | Modality | Size (sample=5k) | Source |
|---------|----------|-----------------|--------|
| Flickr30k | Images + captions | ~400 MB | HuggingFace datasets |
| MS-COCO val | Images + captions | ~900 MB | images.cocodataset.org |

After this step you will see:
```
data/images/flickr/                  ← flickr images
data/processed/flickr_captions.txt   ← image paths + captions
data/images/val2017/                 ← COCO images
data/raw/annotations/captions_train2017.json   ← COCO train captions
data/raw/annotations/captions_val2017.json   ← COCO val captions
```

---

### Step 4 — Build the FAISS indexes

This is the **most time-consuming step** (15–60 minutes depending on hardware).

```bash
# Build both text and image indexes
python scripts/build_index.py --all --batch-size 64

# Or build them separately
python scripts/build_index.py --text    # BERT encoding of passages
python scripts/build_index.py --images  # CLIP encoding of images

# Verify indexes were built correctly
python scripts/build_index.py --verify
```

**Expected output:**
```
INFO: [TextEncoder] Loading model 'sentence-transformers/all-mpnet-base-v2'...
INFO: [IndexBuilder] Building text index: 5000 vectors of dim 768
INFO: Text index saved → indexes/text_index.faiss
INFO: [ImageEncoder] Loading CLIP 'ViT-B/32'...
INFO: [IndexBuilder] Building image index: 2000 vectors of dim 512
INFO: Image index saved → indexes/image_index.faiss
INFO: Metadata saved → indexes/metadata.pkl
```

---

### Step 5 — Run the web interface

```bash
streamlit run app/streamlit_app.py
```

Open your browser at **http://localhost:8501**

---

### Step 6 — Run evaluation (optional)

```bash
# Compare dense retrieval vs BM25 baseline
python scripts/evaluate.py --mode --both
```

**Expected output:**
```
=== BM25 Baseline ===
  P@10        : 0.1980
  R@10        : 0.1750
  MAP         : 0.1340
  MRR         : 0.2610
  nDCG@10     : 0.2050
```

---

## 🔍 How to Use the Search Engine

### Search Modes

| Mode | Query Type | Index Searched | Model Used |
|------|-----------|---------------|------------|
| Text → Text | Text string | Text FAISS | Sentence-BERT |
| Text → Images | Text string | Image FAISS | CLIP text encoder |
| Image → Text | Uploaded image | Text FAISS | CLIP image encoder |
| Image → Images | Uploaded image | Image FAISS | CLIP image encoder |
| Hybrid | Text string | Both indexes | BERT + CLIP + RRF fusion |

### Sidebar Controls

- **Top-k**: How many results to retrieve (5–50)
- **Re-ranker**: Cross-encoder rescores top-k for better precision
- **Query expansion**: Automatically adds synonyms/related words

---

## 🧠 Architecture Overview

```
User Query (text or image)
        ↓
  Query Expansion
        ↓
  Embedding Generation
    ├─ Text  → CLIP ViT-B/32  (512-dim)
    └─ Image → CLIP ViT-B/32  (512-dim)
        ↓
  FAISS ANN Search
    ├─ text.faiss  (IndexFlatIP)
    └─ image.faiss (IndexFlatIP)
        ↓
  Initial Top-k Candidates
        ↓
  Cross-Encoder Re-ranking
    └─ ms-marco-MiniLM-L-6-v2
        ↓
  Final Ranked Results
```

---

## 📊 Datasets Summary

### Flickr30k (Images)
- **Source**: HuggingFace `nlphuji/flickr30k`
- **What it is**: 31,783 images, each with 5 human-written captions
- **We use**: First caption per image as the document "text"
- **Good for**: Text-to-image and image-to-text retrieval

### MS-COCO 2017 (Alternative images)
- **Source**: http://cocodataset.org
- **What it is**: 118K train / 5K val images with 5 captions each
- **We use**: val2017 subset (5,000 images)
- **Good for**: Larger-scale image search experiments

---

## ⚡ Performance Tips

| Situation | Recommendation |
|-----------|---------------|
| Slow encoding | Use GPU: set `device="cuda"` in encoders |
| Very large corpus (>100K) | Use `IVF256,PQ32` index (auto-selected) |
| Better text quality | Switch to `all-mpnet-base-v2` (default) |
| Faster text encoding | Use `all-MiniLM-L6-v2` |
| Better image quality | Switch CLIP to `ViT-L/14` |
| Better re-ranking | Use `cross-encoder/ms-marco-electra-base` |

---

## 🐛 Common Issues

**`ModuleNotFoundError: clip`**
```bash
pip install git+https://github.com/openai/CLIP.git
```

**`No indexes found`**
```bash
python scripts/build_index.py --all
```

**`NLTK resource not found`**
```python
import nltk
nltk.download('all')
```

**Out of memory during encoding**
```bash
python scripts/build_index.py --all --batch-size 16
```

**Streamlit port already in use**
```bash
streamlit run app/streamlit_app.py --server.port 8502
```
